{"study_accession":"PRJNA1143371","secondary_study_accession":"SRP523822","title":"Expansion of peripheral T cell clonotypes predict response in patients with small cell neuroendocrine bladder and prostate cancers treated with chemo-immunotherapy in a phase I clinical trial [bulkRNA-Seq]","description":"To explore the impact of immunotherapy, we report a single institution, dual cohort phase Ib study (NCT 03582475) of platinum-based chemotherapy in combination with PD-1 antagonist pembrolizumab to evaluate safety and preliminary efficacy in patients with small cell bladder and small cell/neuroendocrine prostate cancers. To assess the immunologic basis for responses, single cell gene expression and T cell receptor (TCR) sequencing of serial peripheral blood samples revealed a diverse T cell repertoire with expansion of large clonotypes correlating with response. Overall design: Total tumor RNA sequencing of formalin-fixed paraffin embedded pre-treatment tumor tissue were performed by next-generation sequencing using the Tempus xR assay (Tempus Labs, Chicago, IL), to investigate the cellulor composition and enriched genes.","pubmed":"39536751","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN43000375","study_accession":"PRJNA1143371","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"study","title":"Tumor, Responder Progressed patient208","description":"Tumor, Responder Progressed patient208","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8437132","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-10-27","attributes":[["source_name","tumor"],["tissue","tumor"],["group","Responder Progressed"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR30110375","experiment_accession":"SRX25583236","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":60945006,"base_count":9223569793,"first_public":"2024-10-27","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM8437132: Tumor, Responder